<title>SINGAPORE: Giken Sakata returns to black.</title>
<headline>Giken Sakata returns to black.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   0.03   vs    (4.55)</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	  0.04   vs    (7.88)</p>
<p>    Turnover		   283.41   vs   351.02</p>
<p>    Other income		 0.38   vs     0.10</p>
<p>    Interest expense	   1.36   vs     1.78</p>
<p>    Associates		   0.04   vs     0.10</p>
<p>    Tax			    0.52   vs     0.04</p>
<p>    Minorities		  (0.53)  vs    (0.21)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    nil    vs    (0.24)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    nil    vs     0.24 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Giken Sakata (Singapore) Pte Ltd, a manufacturer of electronic products, said the return from the previous loss was due to continued restructuring and cost saving including divestment of non-strategic assets.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
